	abstract = {The terms orchestration and choreography describe two aspects of emerging standards for creating business processes from multiple Web services. The two terms overlap somewhat, but orchestration refers to an executable business process that can interact with both internal and external Web services. Orchestration always represents control from one parry's perspective. This distinguishes it from choreography, which is more collaborative and allows each involved party to describe its part in the interaction.
