	abstract = {The long-term, 34+ year record of global Landsat remote sensing data is a critical resource to study the Earth system and human impacts on this system. The National Satellite Land Remote Sensing Data Archive ({NSLRSDA}) is charged by public law to: “maintain a permanent,
comprehensive Government archive of global Landsat and other land remote sensing data for long-term monitoring and study of the changing global environment” (U.S. Congress, 1992). The advisory committee for {NSLRSDA} requested a detailed analysis of observation coverage within the U.S.
