	doi = {10.3390/land11091552},
	abstract = {Land-use and land-cover ({LULC}) themes are important for many domains, especially when they process environmental and socio-economic phenomena. The evolution of a land-use database called Open Land Use ({OLU}) started in 2013 and was continued by adapting many user requirements. The goal of this study was to design a new version of the {OLU} database that would better fit the gathered user requirements collected by projects using {LULC} data. A formal definition of the developed data model through Unified Modeling Language ({UML}) class diagrams, a feature catalogue based on {ISO} 19110 and {SQL} scripts for setting up the {OLU} database, are the key achievements of the presented paper. The presented research provides a multi-scale open database of {LULC} information supporting the {DestinE} initiative to develop a very-high-precision digital model of the earth. The novel spatio-temporal thematic approach also lies in modular views of the {OLU} database.},
