	abstract = {The significance of earth observation data spans diverse fields and domains, driving the need for efficient management. Nevertheless, the exponential increase in data volume brings new challenges that complicate processing and storing data. This article proposes an optimized multi-modular service for earth observation data management in response to these challenges. The suggested approach focuses on choosing the optimal configurations for the storage and processing layers to improve the performance and cost-effectiveness of managing data. By employing the recommended optimized strategies, earth observation data can be managed more effectively, resulting in fast data processing and reduced costs.},
